```

**Start order**:
1. Start **Phase 1** immediately. Nothing else can start until Phase 1 is done.
2. When Phase 1 is done → start **Phase 2** and **Phase 3** in parallel.
3. Phase 4 can start as soon as Phase 2.2 (scheme handler factory) has landed AND Phase 3.3 (JSON-RPC registry) has landed. Partial start is allowed — 4.1, 4.2, 4.6 can begin earlier; 4.5 must wait on 3.3; 4.7 absorbs work from 3.10.
4. Phase 5 starts only after Phase 2 and Phase 4 are both fully done.
5. Phase 6 starts only after Phase 5 is fully done.

**Partial-start rule**: a subtask can be started with a reduced scope prompt if only some of its steps are unblocked. Tell the agent explicitly which step numbers to tackle first and which to defer.

