## Done criteria

A subtask is done when **its exit criterion from the plan is met and verified**. Don't mark done on the agent's say-so alone — ask the agent to demonstrate the phase's stated demo before marking complete.

- Phase 1 done: `chrome://hello/` clickable on signed binary, all three OSes.
- Phase 2 done: 5 foundation patches rebase clean; sidecar handshake logs visible.
- Phase 3 done: parity ledger 100% green; existing Playwright suite passes; every handler test green on Bun; preload tests retired.
- Phase 4 done: shared packages shipping; demo regions prove state fan-out; dev harness < 200ms reload; shared test harness runs in CI.
- Phase 5 done: layout grid of labelled placeholders resizable + tabbable; 5.3 feasibility checkpoint passes (real `WebContents` in a slot).
- Phase 6 done: 4 SSO flows pass; ≥ 3 major extensions work; tab switch < 50 ms.

When a phase hits its exit: mark the subtask done (`slay tasks done <subtask-id>`), then start whatever the dependency graph now unblocks.

